---
// "Know where you stand" band: the four read-only view commands.
---

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Know where you stand</span>
    <h2 class="h2">One command to see the whole surface</h2>
    <p class="sub">The plan is always on the tracker, and a handful of read-only views render it back to you, low-res and legible.</p>
    <div class="views">
      <div class="view">
        <div class="vcmd"><span class="s">/trailhead:</span>map</div>
        <h3>The low-res map</h3>
        <p>Destination, the <b>decisions</b> made, the <b>frontier</b> you can take now, and the <b>fog</b> still ahead. One glance at where the project stands.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="view">
        <div class="vcmd"><span class="s">/trailhead:</span>whiteboard</div>
        <h3>The whiteboard</h3>
        <p>The loose, <b>map-less tickets</b> off to the side: what's open, its own frontier, and who holds each one.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="view">
        <div class="vcmd"><span class="s">/trailhead:</span>dashboard</div>
        <h3>The pinned index</h3>
        <p>One <b>pinned issue</b> indexing every open map, the whiteboard, and live counts, always one click away in the repo.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="view">
        <div class="vcmd"><span class="s">/trailhead:</span>inbox</div>
        <h3>Triage what others opened</h3>
        <p>Issues <b>other people filed</b> flow through an inbox; fold the worthwhile ones into the map in place, keeping their authorship.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
